    },
    "A container has to stop before it can be deleted." : {

    },
    "A container is attached to this network. Delete that container, then delete the network." : {

    },
    "A container is using this volume. Stop that container, then delete the volume." : {

    },
    "A container named “%@” already exists here." : {

    },
    "A container’s Docker original is stopped only after its copy here starts successfully, and it is never deleted — if starting fails, the original is started again automatically. Docker must be running during the migration so its data can be read." : {

    },
    "A Port Is Already in Use" : {

    },
    "A published port is already in use — stop whatever is using it (for example, the same stack running in Docker) and try again." : {

    },
    "A stack is a whole app — several containers described by one compose file, managed together. The Stacks area lists each one with its services, live CPU and memory, and a single badge for the whole stack. Start, stop, or restart everything at once, or drill into a single service." : {

    },
